  "purpose": "device.ir.send transmits one infrared code and is acknowledged with no result once the emitter has been handed the last send. encoding is NEC, the only encoding; code is an integer from 0 to 16777215 (0xFFFFFF); repeat is how many more times the Player sends the whole code, about 110 ms apart, an integer from 0 to 10 (0 when absent: the code is sent once). It is a resend of the whole code, not an NEC repeat frame, so a transmitter that can only send whole codes (BrightSign) and one that can send repeat frames (Android) behave alike. A Player that can only transmit (an infrared emitter and no receiver) advertises device.ir.send; one that also receives advertises device.ir, which supports device.ir.send, and may list both.",
